+# Zava Designer Agent — HorizonDB workshop fork
+
+[日本語](README.md)
+
+Provision, initialize and deploy a HorizonDB-backed React application with **`azd up`**. **Azure Container Apps is the default**; a parameter selects App Service instead. The backend calls real HorizonDB functions and managed models.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+Install Azure CLI, Azure Developer CLI 1.37.1+, Node.js 24+ and npm. The PostgreSQL exercises additionally require `psql` 16.15+. ACR builds images in Azure, so local Docker is unnecessary.
+
+Use an Azure Public subscription/region with HorizonDB PostgreSQL 17, two-vCore capacity and AI Model Management for embedding, chat and reranking. Resource creation and RBAC assignment permissions are required: Owner, or Contributor plus RBAC administration. **Review model terms and costs before running.**
+
+```bash
+az login
+azd auth login
+azd env new '<unique-environment>'
+azd env set AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID '<subscription-id>'
+azd env set AZURE_LOCATION '<region-id>'
+azd up
+```
+
+Use letters, digits and hyphens in the environment name and a region ID such as `japaneast`. Authenticate both CLIs with the same account. Changing shared global defaults is unnecessary. Initial database creation and managed-model preparation can take some time.
+
+## What is automated
+
+| Resource | Lab configuration |
+| --- | --- |
+| HorizonDB | PostgreSQL 17, Intel Generation 1, two vCores, one writer, HA disabled |
+| Parameter group | AI, vector, DiskANN, BM25, Durable Pipeline and Apache AGE |
+| Managed models | `default-embedding`, `default-chat`, `default-reranker` |
+| Container Apps | Consumption, 0.5 vCPU / 1 GiB, 0–1 replicas; Node.js 24 serves React and Express |
+| ACR / Log Analytics | Basic registry for remote builds/images; application log storage |
+| Networking | VNet, NAT Gateway, static IPv4, private endpoint and private DNS for Key Vault |
+| Key Vault | Public access disabled; application identity reads only its own DB credential |
+| Initialization | 18 fictional products, 1536-dimensional embeddings, DiskANN/BM25 indexes and style graph |
+
+Hooks associate the custom parameter group after pool creation, restart only for pending static changes, and enable AI Model Management through its update API. Deployment verifies static UI assets, database health and a real six-stage design request.
+
+Generated credentials are not printed or passed in process arguments. They remain in permission-restricted `.azure/<environment>/.env` and Key Vault; never commit environment files. Database access is limited to the client and fixed NAT egress IPv4. Application access is limited to the client IP, discovered with `api.ipify.org`. Set `AZURE_CLIENT_IP` explicitly with `azd env set` if necessary. TLS certificate/hostname validation stays enabled.
+
+Reruns preserve existing products and embeddings. Unexpected catalog counts or unavailable AI features cause explicit errors. This is a temporary lab, not a production availability/network design. Vault purge protection is disabled to allow cleanup of temporary credentials.
+
+**NAT Gateway, ACR, Private Endpoint and other infrastructure incur charges even at zero replicas.** Budget for the database, inference, logs and networking, and clean up after use.
+
+## Select App Service
+
+Set this in an environment that has not been provisioned:
+
+```bash
+azd env set AZURE_HOSTING_TARGET appservice
+azd up
+```
+
+This publishes Node.js source to a Linux B1 plan/Web App and requires B1 provisioning quota. Fixed-egress/private-vault networking is shared with this option; ACR, Container Apps and Log Analytics are not created.
+
+An already provisioned environment cannot change hosts. Create a new environment and configure its subscription/region to switch. The explicit Container Apps value is `containerapp`.
+
+## Use the application
+
+Open the reported URL and click **Design My Room**. Change theme, budget and priorities, then inspect **Agent Details** for real generation, schema inspection, hybrid search, AGE traversal, SQL filtering and reranking traces.
+
+Photos are static demonstration assets. Photo analysis, image generation, 100K products, brand filtering and checkout are not implemented. Managed services perform model inference; Node.js orchestrates six SQL stages and final budget selection. No separate vector database, search service or graph database is needed.
+
+## Staged one-hour workshop
+
+Start with `azd provision`, explain the technology while resources are created, then run `node zava/scripts/psql.mjs` from the parent workshop root. This launches TLS-validated psql without printing credentials. After the SQL exercises, run `azd deploy` here; initialization reuses the existing catalog, embeddings and graph.
+
+Standalone deployment still uses **`azd up` alone**.
+
+## Cleanup
+
+```bash
+azd down --purge
+```
+
+Confirm the selected environment's resource group before approving deletion. This removes the database, application, ACR, logs, vault, NAT Gateway, static IPv4, VNet, private endpoint and private DNS. Verify deletion of the Container Apps-managed group (`ME-...`, from `AZURE_CONTAINER_INFRASTRUCTURE_GROUP`) too. The optional App Service plan/Web App are removed if selected.
+
+Local fork/source remains. If organizational policy prevents vault purge, verify retained state with an administrator.
+
+## Licensing and provenance
+
+Code/assets and newly written README, infrastructure, scripts and data use [MIT](LICENSE). Retained [upstream documentation](README.upstream.md) uses [CC BY-SA 4.0](LICENSE-DOCS).
+
+Upstream: `microsoft/Build26-DEM364-simplify-app-dev-with-cloud-native-postgresql-in-azure-horizondb`, revision `74d448cde1066defc62bb17ae999f68ab1cfa9f2`. The editable local branch is `workshop/azd`; pushing to `upstream` is disabled. No GitHub-hosted fork was created.
